            <div xml:id="d76">

                <pb facs="0149" n="89" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg89"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-08"><hi rendition="#italic">July 8, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received August 23.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2283.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my dispatch No. 2278, of July 1, I
                    inclosed a copy of my proposal to the Tsung-li Yamên to refer the consideration
                    of matters growing out of the Chengtu riots to a commission consisting of
                    certain Chinese officials and an English and American missionary.</p>
                <p>I have now the honor to inclose a translation of the answer of the <pb
                        facs="0150" n="90" xml:id="pg90"/> Yamên to that proposal, from which it
                    will be seen that it has been accepted.</p>
                <p>The personnel of the commission has been, however, modified to the extent that
                    the Chinese members thereof shall consist of the judge, treasurer, and prefect
                    of Chengtu, retaining an Englishman and an American as members. Possibly Her
                    Britannic Majesty’s consul at Chungking may sit on the commission should it meet
                    at that port.</p>
                <p>It is proper to state that should the proceedings before the commission develop
                    the fact that the Viceroy Liu and other local officials failed to do their duty
                    in protecting the foreigners their punishment will be insisted on.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d76-a1.xml" xpointer="d76-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
